  "summary": "The 2026–2027 resource updates (PDBe, CIViC, canSAR, GPCRdb, DGIdb and others) pair content growth with AI tooling and programmatic or agentic interfaces.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is curated biomolecular resources expanding in content while adding AI components and machine-oriented interfaces. PDBe adds literature-mined residue annotations, MD data linked via MDposit, MOLE pore analyses, and API plus MCP agentic access. canSAR 2026 adds ML predictors and agentic-AI protein tools. CIViC 2026 introduces AI-guided curation, Feature entities, Molecular Profiles and ClinVar submission. GPCRdb incorporates Boltz-2 and AlphaFold2-Multimer models alongside ligand interaction data. DGIdb adds Python and R clients, Docker images and versioned releases. On content, HIPPIE 3.0 reaches about 1.2M experimentally supported PPIs with negative training sets. FusionGDB 3.0 covers 156K fusion genes with personalized fusion protein sequences. PRGdb 5.0 applies DREM deep-learning prioritization to 874,967 plant candidate proteins. CiliaHub curates over 2,500 ciliary genes. The IDKG preprint integrates 20 sources into a Neo4j graph for infectious-disease drug discovery. Not every resource adds AI or agentic access.",
